"""Rebuild the assessed notebook with the same reviewed cell sources and no saved outputs."""
import json
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
NOTEBOOK = json.loads("{\"cells\":[{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-00\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"# NLP Final: TF-IDF lost-item candidate ranking\\n\",\"\\n\",\"This notebook has two separate datasets: transcribed monthly inventory totals and a small, fictional matching benchmark. **Only the fictional benchmark is used to train and score matching methods.** A match score suggests records for staff review; it cannot prove ownership or authorize release.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"## Workflow\\n\",\"\\n\",\"1. Define the lost-to-found ranking task and its human-review boundary.\\n\",\"2. Record sources; profile aggregate inventory and prepare controlled examples.\\n\",\"3. Validate columns, IDs, labels, missing values and grouped data splits.\\n\",\"4. Compare a Logistic Regression baseline with TF-IDF and other rankers.\\n\",\"5. Tune on validation data; report held-out accuracy and ranking measures.\\n\",\"6. Inspect explanations and demo the service and Android app.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"**Assessment reading guide:** Sections 1–2 establish the problem and prepare data; sections 3–6 compare methods and evaluate them; sections 7–9 show the operational ranking path, input checks and limitations. For the required live application demonstration, use the authenticated Android service, not the local preview. Existing saved outputs are from the prior benchmark run; new or changed cells must be executed in a clean kernel before submission.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-01\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 1. Transcribed inventory totals\\n\",\"\\n\",\"`data/raw/campus/office_inventory_aggregate.csv` contains 57 category rows from the user-provided June–July and August 2026 summaries: 388 and 299 items. These are aggregate counts, not item reports or match labels, so they describe inventory only. Original names are kept beside normalized labels. The June–July umbrella disposal field is blank in the source and remains unknown. Verify the transcription with the office before submission.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-02\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"import csv\\n\",\"from collections import defaultdict\\n\",\"from pathlib import Path\\n\",\"import sys\\n\",\"# Nimrod — locate the repository whether Jupyter starts in notebooks/ or the root.\\n\",\"ROOT = next((p for p in (Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents)\\n\",\"             if (p / 'scripts/prepare_ranking_benchmark.py').is_file()), None)\\n\",\"if ROOT is None:\\n\",\"    raise FileNotFoundError('Open the notebook from within SemProject_MLEngine.')\\n\",\"if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\\n\",\"    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\\n\",\"inventory_path = ROOT / 'data/raw/campus/office_inventory_aggregate.csv'\\n\",\"with inventory_path.open(encoding='utf-8', newline='') as stream:\\n\",\"    inventory = list(csv.DictReader(stream))\\n\",\"totals = defaultdict(int); category_totals = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))\\n\",\"for row in inventory:\\n\",\"    quantity = int(row['quantity'])\\n\",\"    totals[row['period']] += quantity\\n\",\"    category_totals[row['period']][row['category']] += quantity\\n\",\"print('period | rows | quantity | missing disposal destination')\\n\",\"for period in totals:\\n\",\"    rows = [row for row in inventory if row['period'] == period]\\n\",\"    missing_destination = sum(not row['dispose_to'].strip() for row in rows)\\n\",\"    print(f\\\"{period} | {len(rows)} | {totals[period]} | {missing_destination}\\\")\\n\",\"    print('  category totals:', dict(category_totals[period]))\\n\",\"print('Used for training or scoring: no. The table has no item-level match labels.')\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"nlp-inventory-chart\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\"import pandas as pd\\n\",\"from IPython.display import display\\n\",\"inventory_summary = pd.DataFrame(category_totals).T.fillna(0)\\n\",\"display(inventory_summary)\\n\",\"ax = inventory_summary.plot(kind='bar', figsize=(8, 3.5), rot=0)\\n\",\"ax.set(title='Office inventory quantities by category', xlabel='Reporting period', ylabel='Reported quantity')\\n\",\"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\"plt.show()\"],\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-03\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"from pathlib import Path\\n\",\"from tempfile import TemporaryDirectory\\n\",\"import csv, json\\n\",\"from scripts.prepare_ranking_benchmark import main as prepare\\n\",\"from scripts.validate_ranking_dataset import validate\\n\",\"_NOTEBOOK_TMP = TemporaryDirectory(prefix='nlp-ranking-')\\n\",\"RUN_DIR = Path(_NOTEBOOK_TMP.name)\\n\",\"DATA = RUN_DIR / 'ranking'\\n\",\"prepare(DATA)\\n\",\"audit = validate(DATA)\\n\",\"assert audit['valid'], audit['errors']\\n\",\"print(json.dumps(audit, indent=2))\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-04\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 2. Fictional matching benchmark\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The preparation script creates found reports, lost claims, pair labels and evaluation queries. Its validator checks columns, IDs, references, labels and splits, but not real-world truth. Item groups never cross train, validation and test; the candidate pool has 24 fictional found reports. No-match queries have no relevant found ID.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Training develops the representation/classifier; validation selects settings; testing measures held-out performance. Grouping related examples reduces leakage. There are 8 training, 9 validation and 10 test queries, including one validation and two test queries without a designated match.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-05\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"def read_csv(name):\\n\",\"    with (DATA / name).open(encoding='utf-8', newline='') as stream:\\n\",\"        return list(csv.DictReader(stream))\\n\",\"found = read_csv('found_reports.csv'); lost = read_csv('lost_reports.csv')\\n\",\"labels = read_csv('match_labels.csv'); queries = read_csv('evaluation_queries.csv')\\n\",\"for split in ('train', 'validation', 'test'):\\n\",\"    groups = {r['item_group_id'] for r in found if r['split'] == split}\\n\",\"    print(split, 'item groups:', len(groups), 'matched queries:', sum(q['split']==split and q['has_match']=='1' for q in queries))\\n\",\"print('sources:', sorted({r['source_type'] for r in found}))\\n\",\"print('example:', {k: found[0][k] for k in ('found_id','category','description','source_type')})\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-06\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"from collections import Counter\\n\",\"from statistics import median\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def inspect_table(name, rows, id_field):\\n\",\"    ids = [row.get(id_field, '').strip() for row in rows]\\n\",\"    descriptions = [row.get('description', '').strip() for row in rows]\\n\",\"    categories = Counter(row.get('category', '').strip() or '[missing]' for row in rows)\\n\",\"    print(f'{name}: {len(rows)} rows; duplicate {id_field}: {len(ids) - len(set(ids))}; blank descriptions: {sum(not text for text in descriptions)}')\\n\",\"    print(f'  description characters: min={min(map(len, descriptions))}, median={median(map(len, descriptions))}, max={max(map(len, descriptions))}')\\n\",\"    print('  category counts:', dict(sorted(categories.items())))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"inspect_table('found', found, 'found_id')\\n\",\"inspect_table('lost', lost, 'lost_id')\\n\",\"print('pair-label counts:', dict(Counter(row['label'] for row in labels)))\\n\",\"print('query split counts:', dict(Counter(row['split'] for row in queries)))\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"nlp-split-chart\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"split_order = ['train', 'validation', 'test']\\n\",\"split_counts = pd.Series({s: sum(q['split'] == s for q in queries) for s in split_order})\\n\",\"ax = split_counts.plot(kind='bar', figsize=(5.5, 3), rot=0)\\n\",\"ax.set(title='Benchmark queries by split', ylabel='Queries')\\n\",\"for p in ax.patches:\\n\",\"    ax.annotate(str(int(p.get_height())), (p.get_x() + p.get_width()/2, p.get_height()),\\n\",\"                ha='center', va='bottom')\\n\",\"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\"plt.show()\"],\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-07\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 3. Baseline: Logistic Regression\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Fit a fresh classifier on engineered pair features from the 64 training pairs. This is a comparison model, not the model loaded by the live worker. All results remain synthetic.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The original coursework baseline is retained in [LogisticRegression_Baseline.ipynb](LogisticRegression_Baseline.ipynb). The comparison fits a new Logistic Regression classifier on 64 training pairs using 14 engineered numerical features. The evaluator uses balanced class weights and a fixed random seed; the live worker does not load this classifier.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-08\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"from matching_system.logistic_regression_features import FEATURE_NAMES, pair_features\\n\",\"from scripts.evaluate_ranking_benchmark import as_report\\n\",\"train_labels = [r for r in labels if r['split']=='train']\\n\",\"found_by_id = {r['found_id']: r for r in found}; lost_by_id = {r['lost_id']: r for r in lost}\\n\",\"example = train_labels[0]\\n\",\"features = pair_features(as_report(lost_by_id[example['lost_id']], 'lost'), as_report(found_by_id[example['found_id']], 'found'))\\n\",\"print('training pairs:', len(train_labels), 'features:', list(features))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"# Show the baseline fitting procedure used by the comparison script.\\n\",\"import numpy as np\\n\",\"from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\\n\",\"X_train = np.array([[pair_features(\\n\",\"    as_report(lost_by_id[r['lost_id']], 'lost'),\\n\",\"    as_report(found_by_id[r['found_id']], 'found')\\n\",\")[name] for name in FEATURE_NAMES] for r in train_labels])\\n\",\"y_train = np.array([int(r['label']) for r in train_labels])\\n\",\"baseline = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, class_weight='balanced', random_state=42)\\n\",\"baseline.fit(X_train, y_train)\\n\",\"print('Training matrix:', X_train.shape, '| labels:', dict(zip(*np.unique(y_train, return_counts=True))))\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-09\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 4. Final method: TF-IDF retrieval\\n\",\"\\n\",\"TF-IDF emphasizes words that distinguish reports; unigrams and bigrams capture words and short phrases. Fit vocabulary on training text only. Cosine similarity measures text closeness, not ownership probability.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Example: `BLACK HP Laptop-Charger!` becomes `black hp laptop charger`. Unigrams are individual words; bigrams include `hp laptop` and `laptop charger`. TF-IDF gives more weight to distinctive terms; cosine similarity compares the direction of the vectors. The offline comparison fits on training descriptions only. The operational ranker instead indexes the current found-item inventory using item name plus description (see section 7).\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-10\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\\n\",\"from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\\n\",\"from matching_system.nlp_retrieval import normalize_report_text\\n\",\"training_text = [normalize_report_text(r['description']) for r in found + lost if r['split']=='train']\\n\",\"vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(ngram_range=(1,2), strip_accents='unicode').fit(training_text)\\n\",\"query_text = normalize_report_text(lost_by_id['l-g017']['description'])\\n\",\"found_text = normalize_report_text(found_by_id['f-g017']['description'])\\n\",\"similarity = cosine_similarity(vectorizer.transform([query_text]), vectorizer.transform([found_text]))[0,0]\\n\",\"print('vocabulary size:', len(vectorizer.vocabulary_), 'example cosine:', round(float(similarity), 4))\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-11\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 5. Validation and model selection\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Compare keyword overlap, structured attributes, Logistic Regression, TF-IDF and a hybrid on the same candidate pool. Choose the hybrid weight and no-match cutoff on validation data. Keep the test split for final reporting only.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The experimental cutoff is not the operational rejection policy. The current worker returns positive lexical similarities, up to five per ranker call. Hybrid weighting is an offline experiment; the worker has no hybrid reranking.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-12\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"from scripts.evaluate_ranking_benchmark import main as evaluate\\n\",\"import contextlib\\n\",\"import io\\n\",\"# Keep the long diagnostic JSON in the results file, not on the presentation screen.\\n\",\"with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\\n\",\"    results = evaluate(data_dir=DATA, result_path=RUN_DIR/'ranking_benchmark.json')\\n\",\"print('selected TF-IDF weight:', results['hybrid']['tfidf_weight_selected_on_validation'])\\n\",\"print('training feature count:', len(results['logistic_regression']['features']))\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-13\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 6. Held-out results\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Top-1 accuracy counts matched queries ranked first. Recall@5 counts queries with a correct item in the first five. MRR rewards higher ranks. False suggestions count no-match queries whose top score passes a validation-set cutoff. Denominators are printed. These are fictional benchmark scores, not campus recovery rates.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Top-1, Recall@5 and MRR use eight matched test queries; the false-suggestion counts use two no-match queries. Offline MRR uses the full 24-candidate ordering. The operational top-five MRR below is explicitly truncated.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-14\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"print('method | Top-1 accuracy (matched queries) | Recall@5 | MRR | no-match false suggestions')\\n\",\"for name, item in results['methods'].items():\\n\",\"    test = item['test']\\n\",\"    print(f\\\"{name} | {test['top1_accuracy']:.3f} ({test['matched_queries']}) | {test['recall_at_5']:.3f} | {test['mrr']:.3f} | {item['test_no_match_false_suggestions']}/{item['test_no_match_denominator']}\\\")\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"nlp-metrics-chart\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"summary = pd.DataFrame([\\n\",\"    {'Method': name, 'Top-1': info['test']['top1_accuracy'],\\n\",\"     'Recall@5': info['test']['recall_at_5'], 'MRR': info['test']['mrr'],\\n\",\"     'False suggestions': f\\\"{info['test_no_match_false_suggestions']}/{info['test_no_match_denominator']}\\\"}\\n\",\"    for name, info in results['methods'].items()\\n\",\"]).set_index('Method')\\n\",\"display(summary.round(3))\\n\",\"ax = summary[['Top-1', 'Recall@5']].plot(kind='bar', figsize=(9, 3.7), rot=15)\\n\",\"ax.set(title='Offline benchmark: matched test queries (n=8)', ylabel='Fraction', ylim=(0, 1.08))\\n\",\"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\"plt.show()\"],\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-15\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 7. Explanation and input checks\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The preview returns text similarity, fact statuses and staff guidance. This in-process check exercises explanation and validation logic only; it does not test HTTP, Firebase or Android. Similarity is not a probability.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The ranker determines order from textual similarity. Knowledge agents add category, location and date evidence and staff guidance after retrieval; these facts do not currently rerank candidates.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-16\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"from pydantic import ValidationError\\n\",\"from matching_system.api import PreviewRequest, preview_matches\\n\",\"request = PreviewRequest(item_name='Metal water bottle',description='Blue bottle with a scratched lid',category_id='metal_water_bottle',location_id='msb',event_date='2026-11-10',limit=3)\\n\",\"body = preview_matches(request)\\n\",\"print('status:', body['status'], 'first ID:', body['matches'][0]['found_report_id'])\\n\",\"print('explanation:', body['matches'][0]['explanation'])\\n\",\"for label, values in [('blank description', {'item_name':'Water bottle','description':''}), ('invalid calendar date', {'item_name':'Water bottle','description':'Blue bottle','event_date':'2026-02-30'})]:\\n\",\"    try:\\n\",\"        PreviewRequest(**values)\\n\",\"    except ValidationError:\\n\",\"        print(label + ': rejected')\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-runtime-evaluation\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"### 7A. Operational matching pipeline evaluation\\n\",\"\\n\",\"This separate check calls the actual `service.inference.TfidfMatcher` used by the Android worker on the same frozen 24-record inventory and ten held-out queries. It fits the found inventory only, returns up to five positive-scoring candidates and applies the existing knowledge agents. The benchmark has no separate item-name column, so the adapter leaves it blank rather than inventing names. This measures the retrieval path for new lost reports, not Firestore, worker scheduling, new-found-report reranking or Android connectivity.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Compare Top-1 and Recall@5 with the offline table. MRR@5 assigns zero to missing candidates; it is not directly comparable with the offline full-list MRR. A no-match false suggestion here means any candidate is returned under the live ranker's positive-score policy, not the offline experimental threshold. Results are generated by the following cell, not hard-coded.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"id\":\"nlp-runtime-metrics\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"from service.inference import TfidfMatcher\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def runtime_row(row, kind):\\n\",\"    return {'id': row[f'{kind}_id'], 'report_type': kind,\\n\",\"            'description': row['description'], 'item_name': row.get('item_name', ''),\\n\",\"            'category_id': row.get('category') or None,\\n\",\"            'location_id': row.get('last_seen_location' if kind == 'lost' else 'location') or None,\\n\",\"            'event_date': row.get('date_lost' if kind == 'lost' else 'event_date') or None}\\n\",\"\\n\",\"pool = json.loads((DATA / 'candidate_pools.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\\n\",\"matcher = TfidfMatcher()\\n\",\"details = []\\n\",\"for q in queries:\\n\",\"    if q['split'] != 'test':\\n\",\"        continue\\n\",\"    inventory_rows = [runtime_row(found_by_id[fid], 'found') for fid in pool[q['candidate_pool_id']]]\\n\",\"    ranked = matcher.recommend(runtime_row(lost_by_id[q['lost_id']], 'lost'), inventory_rows)\\n\",\"    ids = [m['found_report_id'] for m in ranked]\\n\",\"    relevant = set(filter(None, q['relevant_found_ids'].split('|')))\\n\",\"    positions = [i + 1 for i, fid in enumerate(ids) if fid in relevant]\\n\",\"    details.append({'query': q['query_id'], 'has_match': bool(relevant),\\n\",\"                    'first_rank': min(positions) if positions else None,\\n\",\"                    'recall5': len(positions)/len(relevant) if relevant else None,\\n\",\"                    'candidate_count': len(ids),\\n\",\"                    'top_score': ranked[0]['text_similarity'] if ranked else None,\\n\",\"                    'top_candidate': ids[0] if ids else None,\\n\",\"                    'explanation': ranked[0]['explanation'] if ranked else 'No lexical candidates'})\\n\",\"matched = [d for d in details if d['has_match']]\\n\",\"unmatched = [d for d in details if not d['has_match']]\\n\",\"assert len(matched) == 8 and len(unmatched) == 2\\n\",\"print('Operational model:', matcher.version)\\n\",\"print('Top-1:', sum(d['first_rank'] == 1 for d in matched)/len(matched))\\n\",\"print('Recall@5:', sum(d['recall5'] for d in matched)/len(matched))\\n\",\"print('MRR@5:', sum(1/d['first_rank'] if d['first_rank'] else 0 for d in matched)/len(matched))\\n\",\"print('No-match queries with suggestions:', sum(d['candidate_count'] > 0 for d in unmatched), '/', len(unmatched))\\n\",\"display(pd.DataFrame(details).drop(columns='explanation'))\\n\",\"print('Example explanation:', details[0]['explanation'])\"],\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-17\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 8. Optional live HTTP check\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Start the local API with `python -m uvicorn matching_system.api:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001`, then set `NLP_LIVE_HTTP_DEMO=1` before running this cell. It checks valid text, blank text and an invalid date. The local preview is not the authenticated Android workflow; see the Android repository's presentation guide for that demo.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Use port 8001 so the preview cannot be confused with the authenticated `service.api:app` on port 8000. Saved output from the earlier run indicates that this optional cell was skipped. The application demonstration must separately exercise actual report submission, worker results and mobile explanations.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"execution_count\":null,\"id\":\"nlp-final-18\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"source\":[\"import os\\n\",\"import json\\n\",\"from urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\\n\",\"from urllib.request import Request, urlopen\\n\",\"\\n\",\"def post_preview(payload):\\n\",\"    req = Request('http://127.0.0.1:8001/preview/matches', data=json.dumps(payload).encode('utf-8'), headers={'Content-Type':'application/json'}, method='POST')\\n\",\"    try:\\n\",\"        with urlopen(req, timeout=5) as response:\\n\",\"            return response.status, json.loads(response.read().decode('utf-8'))\\n\",\"    except HTTPError as error:\\n\",\"        return error.code, json.loads(error.read().decode('utf-8'))\\n\",\"\\n\",\"if os.environ.get('NLP_LIVE_HTTP_DEMO') == '1':\\n\",\"    valid = {'item_name':'Metal water bottle','description':'Blue bottle with a scratched lid','category_id':'metal_water_bottle','location_id':'msb','event_date':'2026-11-10','limit':3}\\n\",\"    status, result = post_preview(valid)\\n\",\"    print('valid request:', status, result['status'], 'candidate count:', len(result['matches']))\\n\",\"    print('first explanation:', result['matches'][0]['explanation'] if result['matches'] else 'No candidate in the demo inventory')\\n\",\"    print('blank description:', post_preview({**valid, 'description':''})[0])\\n\",\"    print('invalid date:', post_preview({**valid, 'event_date':'2026-02-30'})[0])\\n\",\"else:\\n\",\"    print('Live HTTP check skipped. Start the local API and set NLP_LIVE_HTTP_DEMO=1 to run it.')\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-demo-checklist\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"### 8A. Required application demonstration (ICS 3202)\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Use the Android application with the authenticated FastAPI service and Firebase matching worker. Keep a prepared fictional office inventory and verified test accounts. Demonstrate two different valid descriptions (for example HP versus Dell charger), an invalid blank description or future date, and the actual ranked result and explanation. If available, show a no-match result. Explain how wording changes the lexical ranking and how fact checks help staff review it. All three presenters must be present with cameras on for the 3–6 minute demo. A preview response, notebook output, or passing APK build is not proof of this workflow.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Record the actual observed candidate IDs/scores and errors during rehearsal; do not substitute invented results.\"]},{\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"id\":\"nlp-final-19\",\"metadata\":{},\"source\":[\"## 9. Interpretation and limits\\n\",\"\\n\",\"The structured and hybrid methods score perfectly on eight fictional matched test queries because the generator reuses category and colour fields. TF-IDF misses paraphrases and flags both fictional no-match queries. These tiny constructed results reveal benchmark weaknesses; they are not real-world rates.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"Before claiming campus performance, collect permitted, independently verified item pairs and keep a separate holdout. The team must verify the aggregate transcription, review synthetic examples and labels, run the Android demo and approve the notebook.\\n\",\"\\n\",\"TF-IDF remains the lightweight operational prototype, not the winner of this comparison. Do not claim that validation proves it is superior. The next improvements are operationally aligned evaluation, validated rejection and paraphrase handling, independent item-pair labels and a verified application demonstration.\"]}],\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3.12\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\",\"version\":\"3.12\"}},\"nbformat\":4,\"nbformat_minor\":5}")
(ROOT / "notebooks" / "NLP_Final.ipynb").write_text(json.dumps(NOTEBOOK, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
